                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Infectonator 3 is interesting. It's a fun game, but I feel like it's broken, maybe from degrading over time just because of some deprecated code, or a discrepancy with the operating system I'm on, or something like that.\r\n\r\nI have an old save from 2019, and the game is radically different on there, so most of the game must be generated on the fly, on a file somewhere. The way panic works in the save was preferable, but everything was VERY easy because the cure didn't exist back then. Or, if it did, it just didn't exist in that old save.\r\n\r\nPanic now is very explosive. You can't seem to infect a whole continent without it blowing up first. Maybe that makes the game better in that you don't have to grind as much, but wasn't that the point of the first few Infectonators? I dunno.\r\n\r\nThe game has some gameplay modifiers and global leaderboards to encourage replayability, but I'm 90% sure that because of those aforementioned local game generation points, most of the top scorers are just cheating. After a regular playthrough, I usually get ~500,000 points. The top scorers are in the billions and hundred millions. Maybe the modifiers are multiplicative in the way that they are in LEGO games, but I doubt it.",
